{# ================================================================
   AI Governance and Guardrails
   Cloud Security Alliance (CSA) Birmingham · September 8, 2026
   Birmingham, AL · 50 minutes · in-person

   Modern-engine orchestration layer. This file chooses the brand and the
   slide order; it contains no HTML. Every rendered slide comes from a
   macro under modules/<topic>/ so other decks can reuse it.

   ── Structure (2026-09-07) ──────────────────────────────────────
   Four parts, in the audience's own words. "Governance" is a word this
   room already recognises, so the deck uses it rather than teaching a
   new vocabulary:

     1. What governance is      — make rules, put them in the process,
                                  see if they are followed
     2. Good AI rules           — making rules a machine will actually use
     3. Enforcing them          — putting them in the process
     4. Seeing when they aren't — detection and observability

   Deliberately NOT in this deck: XACML, PAP/PDP/PIP/PEP, and control-
   family vocabulary. The reference architecture is real and the macros
   for it still exist in modules/guardrails/policy-as-code.j2, but naming
   it here costs the room the thread. See that module's header.

   Part 3 ends with the scorecard flip-through — six controls, five
   dimensions, one scale — which is the spine of the talk's argument that
   nothing scores well across the board.

   Part 4 is thinner than parts 1-3 and is known to be; it is the next
   thing to flesh out.

   50 minutes ≈ 43 of slides + 7 of questions. At 32 slides that is
   ~80 seconds each. Trim candidates are marked TRIM below.

   Modules that resolve the brand pack themselves are imported WITH CONTEXT
   — without it `branding` is undefined at load time and the path collapses
   to modules/branding//primitives.j2. See AGENTS.md.
   ================================================================ #}

